  "factCheck": {
    "status": "verified",
    "by": "HeyMariner daily desk",
    "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
    "notes": "UK P&I (15 Apr 2026): jamming = loss of signal, usually recognisable as systems fail; spoofing = wrong but believable fix, alarms may not activate; indicators: position jumps, SOG differing from log speed, gyro heading differing from COG, AIS targets implausible, echo sounder not matching charted depths; actions: radar ranges and bearings, visual fixes, echo sounder, dead reckoning, involve the Master, treat AIS with caution (other vessels may be affected), report interference (e.g. USCG NAVCEN); GNSS never the sole source of position. IMO-ICAO-ITU joint statement confirms rising jamming/spoofing and SOLAS V/19 position-fixing carriage. The half-mile offset in the hook is an illustrative scenario. Reporting channels depend on area, flag and company SMS."
  },
